From: rx550-g5
Subject: [PATCH] libkworkspace: read _KDE_SCREEN_INDEX as a 32-bit value (fix big-endian)

OutputOrderWatcher (X11) dereferenced the uint8_t * returned by
xcb_randr_get_output_property_data(), reading only the first byte of the format-32
_KDE_SCREEN_INDEX value. On big-endian hosts that is the high byte (0), so every output
counted as disabled, the output order was empty and plasmashell created no desktop or panel
views (black screen with a cursor on Plasma X11, ppc64 Power Mac G5).

xcb returns format-32 property data in host byte order; copy the full 32-bit value.

--- a/libkworkspace/outputorderwatcher.cpp
+++ b/libkworkspace/outputorderwatcher.cpp
@@ -7,6 +7,8 @@
 
 #include "outputorderwatcher.h"
 
+#include <cstring>
+
 #include <config-X11.h>
 
 #include <algorithm>
@@ -264,7 +266,11 @@
             return;
         }
 
-        const uint32_t order = *xcb_randr_get_output_property_data(orderReply.data());
+        // xcb_randr_get_output_property_data() returns uint8_t *: dereferencing it reads only the
+        // first byte of the format-32 value, which is the high byte on big-endian hosts (always 0
+        // there, so every output looked disabled and plasmashell created no desktop or panel).
+        uint32_t order;
+        memcpy(&order, xcb_randr_get_output_property_data(orderReply.data()), sizeof(order));
 
         if (order > 0) { // 0 is the special case for disabled, so we ignore it
             orderMap.emplace_back(order,
